WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.808
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.620
RETO MEIER: Hi, I'm Reto Meier,
Google Developer Advocate,

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.870
and I'm still here
with Dave Renson,

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:12.960
director of Customer
Reliability Engineering.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.780
So, Dave, I've always
thought of SREs

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.997
as the first responders
in the computing world.

00:00:16.997 --> 00:00:19.080
When everything is catching
fire and falling down,

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.880
you guys are running in.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:23.580
Has there ever been a situation
where you wanted to turn around

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:24.840
and run the other way?

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:26.370
DAVE RENSON: You
mean, like, when

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:28.710
a hurricane was threatening
to wipe most of the Eastern

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:29.670
seaboard off the map?

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.630
RETO MEIER: Yes,
exactly like that.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:34.020
What does preparation for
something like that look like?

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.695
Inflatable life
rafts, life jackets?

00:00:36.695 --> 00:00:38.820
DAVE RENSON: It's a little
more involved than that.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:40.980
But, if you want to
hear the whole story,

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.940
and more, join us
at Google Next,

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:45.390
at the 5th Nine Lounge,
a dedicated space

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:47.820
for SRE and DevOps people,
where you'll hear all the

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:50.580
wonderful, wild, wacky,
sometimes just plain weird

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:53.040
stories of what it's like to
run a production system at web

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:53.720
scale.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.678
RETO MEIER: We look
forward to seeing you then.

00:00:55.678 --> 00:00:58.520
[MUSIC PLAYING]

